<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Afsharid Empire</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Afsharid dynasty, Afsharids, Afsharid</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Afsharid Empire was the Iranian state founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nader-shah">Nader Shah</a>, who deposed the last Safavid ruler in 1736. Nader built a powerful army, defeated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afghans">Afghans</a>, and sacked <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi">Delhi</a> in 1739, but his rule was harsh and fiscally exhausting. After his assassination in 1747 the empire fragmented, with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zand-dynasty">Zand dynasty</a> taking much of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a> while Afsharid rulers held on in Khurasan.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/afsharid-empire.jpg" alt="Afsharid Empire" width="320" height="192" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Orange Tuesday · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Afsharid_Imperial_Standard_(3_Stripes).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
